# Development Workflow

## Core Documents

Every project uses these two documents. They are the minimum for tracking work.

| Document | Purpose | Updated when |
|---|---|---|
| `docs/PLAN.md` | Sprint roadmap, pending work only | Sprint boundaries, new work added/removed |
| `docs/CHANGELOG.md` | Completed work by sprint, outcomes, decisions | Items completed — moved from PLAN.md |

## Optional Documents

Adopt these when the project's size or complexity justifies them. Don't create them preemptively.

| Document | When to adopt | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `docs/PRD.md` | Multi-phase product with stakeholders | Product requirements, goals, phases, target audience |
| `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` | 3+ services or complex component topology | System overview, diagrams, component topology |
| `docs/adrs/NNN-slug.md` | Non-trivial technical decisions worth recording | Architecture decisions with context and trade-offs |
| `docs/FUTURE_EXPLORATIONS.md` | Active backlog of out-of-scope ideas | Post-PoC themes, exploration backlog |

## Lifecycle Rules

- **Starting new work?** Read `PLAN.md` to find the current sprint and pick a pending item.
- **Completed a sprint item?** Move it from `PLAN.md` to `CHANGELOG.md` with key outcomes.
- **Made an architecture decision?** If the project uses ADRs, write one in `docs/adrs/` and reference it in `CHANGELOG.md`.
- **Exploring something outside current sprint?** Note it in `FUTURE_EXPLORATIONS.md` if it exists, otherwise add a "Future" section in `PLAN.md`.
- **Don't duplicate** — each fact lives in one document and others link to it.

## ADR Conventions

Only applies to projects that have adopted ADRs.

- **Path:** `docs/adrs/NNN-lowercase-kebab-topic.md` (zero-padded to 3 digits)
- **Next number:** check existing files in `docs/adrs/`, increment the highest by 1
- **H1:** `# ADR-NNN: Short Descriptive Title`
- **Sections:** Status, Date, Context (with options considered), Decision, Rationale, Trade-offs, Consequences

## Format Conventions

### PLAN.md
```
# Plan: <Project Name>

**Status:** Sprint N (in progress)
**Date:** YYYY-MM-DD
```
- ASCII progress bar per sprint
- Conventions line: `[ ]` = pending | `[!]` = blocked | **Gate** = required criterion
- Only pending/in-progress work lives here — completed items go to CHANGELOG.md

### CHANGELOG.md
```
# Changelog: <Project Name>
```
- Sections by sprint: `## Sprint N — <Theme>`
- Each sprint has: **Date**, **Status**, **Key Outcomes**, and optionally a **Decisions** table linking ADRs
